Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.109 --> 00:00:04.430
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and next week
Doctor Who Series 8 premieres.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.490
Congrats to anyone who’s made it to the
World Tour so far, some of you have been sending

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.490
me really awesome pics on twitter and facebook.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.490
The next stop as of the day I’m posting
this is New York.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.639
I live in Los Angeles so I won’t be able
to get arrested trying to tackle Peter Capaldi

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:17.390
with hugs but if one of you guys wants to
try tweet the pictures before you get handcuffed.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:22.040
They just released a proper trailer for Episode
1 Deep Breath so this video will be a breakdown

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.080
of the new things in that and we’ve also
learned the titles from all of the regular

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.080
episodes.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.080
There are 12.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.250
The 13th is the christmas special but we don’t
know anything about that yet.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.720
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I do Doctor Who video every week.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.340
And I’m doing a weekly Doctor Who giveaway.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.570
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.570
Details in the description too.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.570
So let’s start with the Deep Breath Trailer.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.810
A lot of it is familiar footage and because
it jumps around in the episode I’m going

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.960
to reorganize things from the same scenes
as I go along.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:48.960
Here we go:

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.050
Starting with Dinosaur’s in London.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:54.000
I know some of you weren’t really taken
with Dinosaurs on a Spaceship but as much

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.550
as the T-Rex is comedy.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:59.540
It’s sheer size makes you think less of
Trikey and more of Jurassic Park.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.930
Fun Fact: Gallifrey, Mondas and Skaro all
used to have their own species of Dinosaurs.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.229
The Gallifreyan ones were called Gigantosaurs.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:07.229
They only appeared in the comics.

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:11.210
The Skaro ones were just triceratops with
one big horn and the Mondas ones were pretty

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.479
much like the earth dinosaurs since Mondas
was Earth’s twin planet.

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:17.521
The Mondas cybermen even converted some of
the dinosaurs into cybermen to use as mounts.

00:01:17.521 --> 00:01:24.180
I don’t think this dinosaur is connected
to any of the villains this season, I think

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.440
it’s just there to introduce Capaldi with
some flair, but the Doctor does speak Dinosaur

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.580
and I’m not talking about Silurian, Vastra’s
native language.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.920
He can speak to big dinosaurs like the T-Rex.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.850
I don’t know if they’ll actually show
this but I think it’s kind of funny.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.700
Here’s the Doctor out of Matt Smith’s
costume but not yet in his new one, this episode

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.270
is the transition from Smith to Capaldi, so
naturally he has to get into his new outfit.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:51.970
But the promo pics we’ve seen and the other
trailer footage show him wearing a victorian

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:59.050
outfit that’s different from what his Doctor
Costume will be.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:03.159
This is what the official costume is, presumably
he’ll be in it by the end of the first episode.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:06.320
Smith changed his appearance a few times during
the Christmas Special.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:17.560
The way I see it is you have the anachronistic
Matt Smith costume.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.250
Young man in very old timey clothes and now
we’re actually way back in Victorian era

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.340
when those clothes would have been totally
normal.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:31.220
Cut to old man appropriately dressed in old
man’s clothes.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:38.590
All of the interview quotes I’ve been seeing
from the World Tour have been about how no-nonsense

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.870
Capaldi is going to be.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.231
Most of the interviews sound like they’re
meant for people who have never read doctor

00:02:42.231 --> 00:02:46.090
who, because I feel like anyone who watched
the 50th Anniversary and saw that clip of

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.420
his eyes, knew exactly what his personality
was going to be.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.250
You can let me know if you agree, but I just
thought he was going to be a badass.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.190
The next montage sets up the action of the
episode, them dealing with the Dinosaur, the

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.810
mysterious Robot Man and the fact the Doctor
is still delirious from his regeneration.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.560
What the Doctor says in case you have trouble
understanding him when he talks really fast

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:11.920
in his scottish accent is “The Question
is, Have there been any similar Murders?”.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.180
There was a rumor that Jack the Ripper would
be involved in the episode and I haven’t

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.180
seen any evidence that he is.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.260
But the rumors might have been referring to
the robot man.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:24.700
Vastra said she killed and ate Jack the Ripper
during Good Man Goes to War, series 6 episode

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.700
7.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.349
So I’m pretty sure it’s not him that made
that big explosion.

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:33.340
I like that Vastra implies that no matter
how addled the Doctor’s mind is from regeneration,

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.260
he automatically hones in on trouble.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.959
It looks like we’ll get another badass Vastra
and Jenny battle.

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:42.020
They got a pretty good one during Crimson
Horror too.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:47.330
That was series 7 episode 12.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:51.330
I like that they gave Clara the Doctor’s
“You’ve redecorated line”.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:56.690
Most people probably remember this from the
50th last year, but the second doctor originated

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:57.690
it.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:01.200
The first time he said it was during the three
doctor’s special when he saw the third doctor’s

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.540
tardis, then again in the five doctors special
inside the UNIT headquarters to Brigadier

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.800
Lethbridge-Stewart, then Matt Smith said it
to Craig when he saw his house in Closing

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:15.190
Time Series 6 Episode 12 and then most recently
David Tennant said it to Matt Smith when he

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.410
saw his TARDIS.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:23.870
Clara is referencing the Book Shelves mostly.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:27.990
I think Matt Smith did have bookshelves and
paintings inside the control room after he

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.719
redecorated before he met Clara in the 2012
christmas special.

00:04:31.719 --> 00:04:34.389
There were also bookshelves inside the seventh
doctor’s TARDIS.

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:35.789
It was more victorian looking.

00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:39.499
I think it’s a nice easter egg since Capaldi’s
first episode is during the victorian era.

00:04:39.499 --> 00:04:42.460
I guess we’ll find out if the bookshelves
stick.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.189
I think the footage we saw of them in the
previous trailers was from the first few episodes.

00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:49.990
I can’t wait to get a better look inside.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.909
Structurally though it’s the same as Matt
Smith’s final TARDIS, just new decorations.

00:04:51.909 --> 00:04:55.960
I think that Capaldi’s smile is just him
acknowledging the humor of her taking what

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.360
should be his line.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:16.119
And now on to episode titles I’m just going
to present all these as a montage with text

00:05:16.119 --> 00:05:22.710
instead of reading them out loud.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.710
Here we go:

